RenGL is free to use for games and applications whose source code is public, and for
non-commercial work. Closed-source commercial products need a Commercial License. Nobody
may sell or otherwise commercialize RenGL itself.

This is a source-available license. It is not an OSI-approved open-source license.


1. DEFINITIONS

"RenGL" means this software: its source code, binaries, documentation, build files and
bundled resources that the Licensor owns, in any version released under this License.

"Modified Version" means RenGL after you have changed, extended, translated or forked it,
or any work that contains copied portions of RenGL's source code.

"Application" means a program, game or other work that uses RenGL, whether by calling it,
linking to it or bundling it, and that is not itself a Modified Version or an Engine
Product.

"Engine Product" means a product or service whose main purpose is to give developers
functionality similar to RenGL's: a game engine, rendering or UI framework, widget
toolkit, library, SDK, editor, or asset pipeline. Whether it is made by modifying RenGL or
by wrapping or re-exporting it, if developers are meant to build on it, it is an Engine
Product.

"Public Source" means the complete source code of an Application (everything needed to
build and run it, other than the items in Section 3.3), made available to the general
public: online, free of charge, without registration, for as long as the Application is
distributed or offered, under a license that lets anyone at least read, copy, build and
modify it for their own use.

"Open Application" means an Application whose Public Source is available as required by
Section 3.

"Commercial Use" means any use of RenGL, or of an Application, that is intended to produce
or does produce revenue or other compensation, directly or indirectly. That includes
selling copies, subscriptions, in-app purchases, advertising, sponsored placement,
paid services, use inside a product a company sells, and use by a company for client
work. It does not include voluntary donations that do not give the donor access to
anything the public cannot get. Use of RenGL in teaching, research, hobby projects and
free software released without any revenue is not Commercial Use.

"Commercial License" means a separate written agreement signed or issued by the Licensor.


2. FREE USE

Subject to this License, you may use, copy, and run RenGL, and create and distribute
Applications, free of charge, for any purpose that is not Commercial Use.

You may do this with closed source for non-commercial work. You do not have to publish
the source of an Application you do not commercialize.


3. COMMERCIAL USE OF OPEN APPLICATIONS

3.1  You may make Commercial Use of an Application, including selling it, without a
     Commercial License and without paying the Licensor, if and only if it is an Open
     Application.

3.2  You must publish the Public Source when you first distribute or offer the Application
     commercially, and keep it current: each released version must have matching Public
     Source available no later than the release. You may choose the license for your own
     source code, provided it satisfies the Public Source definition. You do not have to
     license your Application under this License.

3.3  The Public Source does not have to include (a) art, audio, video, fonts, story and
     other creative content that is not code, (b) code you do not have the right to
     publish, such as a platform holder's SDK, and (c) server-side code that never leaves
     your servers. If you leave something out, the Application must still build and run
     with substitutes.

3.4  You may bundle RenGL, in unmodified or modified form, in the distribution of an Open
     Application, subject to Section 5. The parts of RenGL you bundle stay under this
     License; the rest of your Application stays under yours.


4. COMMERCIAL USE OF CLOSED APPLICATIONS

If an Application is not an Open Application, you need a Commercial License before you
make any Commercial Use of it. Contact the Licensor at [CONTACT EMAIL OR URL]. The
Licensor decides the fee and terms of a Commercial License and may refuse to grant one.

Making Commercial Use without a Commercial License, or after a Commercial License has
ended, is a violation of this License.


5. NO COMMERCIALIZING RENGL ITSELF

Whether or not you publish your source, you may not, without a Commercial License:

(a) sell, license, rent, lease or otherwise charge for RenGL or a Modified Version, alone
    or as part of a bundle, or charge for access to it (this includes paid forks, paid
    mirrors, paid builds, and packaging it for sale on a marketplace);
(b) offer RenGL or a Modified Version as a paid, ad-supported or otherwise monetized
    service, such as hosted or managed use, where the service is substantially RenGL;
(c) distribute an Engine Product commercially;
(d) sublicense RenGL to anyone for a fee, or let a third party do any of the above.

You may charge for an Open Application, and for work done in making one for a client,
provided the Public Source requirement is met. You may recover the reasonable cost of
physical media. You may be paid for teaching, writing about or supporting RenGL as long
as you do not hand over RenGL as the thing being paid for.

Engine Products that are free of charge and under this License are allowed.


6. MODIFIED VERSIONS

6.1  You may modify RenGL and share your Modified Version publicly, provided that you:
     (a) license the whole Modified Version, as far as you have the right to, under this
         License, and make its source code available;
     (b) mark your changes and the date you made them, so they are not mistaken for the
         Licensor's work;
     (c) keep every copyright, license and attribution notice;
     (d) do not use the name "RenGL" in a way that suggests your version is the Licensor's
         official release. You may say it is "based on RenGL".

6.2  Sections 3, 4 and 5 apply to a Modified Version. A Modified Version bundled in an
     Open Application is covered by Section 3.4.


7. NOTICES AND ATTRIBUTION

When you distribute RenGL or an Application containing it, include this License and the
third-party notices that come with RenGL, in the distribution, on a documentation page, or
inside the Application's about or credits screen. You do not have to show a logo or splash
screen.


